# Chroma content pack Politics: WORLD-ONLY moments (moments 64 to 71 of MOMENTS-BRIEF.md, "World-only moments"): four
# that belong to the tribal world and four that belong to the magic world (worlds.py, WORLD_ONLY_POLITICS). Syntax:
# header of chroma-library/build.py. Rules: library-spec.md. Names in title:, grants:, drops: and the rest come from
# politics/catalogue.py, core/reach.py and the base catalogue. Each moment carries `only:` and that world's line alone;
# its scenes are written for that world (scene tribal ..., scene magic ...), so the game tells them only there.
# Each life event is even on its own: alpha even, stakes 1.0, the five one-color options plus the combination set named
# in its header comment. Each world's four moments use both halves of two combination lines (tribal: D5 triads and D2
# pairs; magic: D6 triads and D1 pairs), so the pack stays color-even in every world.
# The tribal world has no magic (library-spec.md): signs, dreams and rites are how the band reads and decides, and
# nothing in these moments says the spirits truly act. In the magic world every supernatural way is one choice among
# ordinary ones, and each has a price (a mark, a binding, a closed: line with a backfire). No option here is the
# person's own spell: the oracle, the thing under the hill, the Order's mages, a hedge-witch and the old healer do the
# magic, so no act needs an awakened gift (the catalogue has no name for one yet).
# per_year is the yearly rate per eligible person (whoever holds a title in holds:); every figure is an estimate.

# ================================================================ tribal world
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 64. an omen at the council fire (triads D5a)
# The band is weighing who will be heard, so each one-color option is a way to be chosen now, at like chances; the
# triads are the other answers. As with 'polling day in the ward', the band decides, not the means.

== an omen at the council fire
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: council candidate
per_year: 0 0 .1 .1 .1 .1
drivers: harsh+.2 unrest+.2
times: per council candidate in the tribal world: about 1 candidacy in 10 meets a sign the band reads for or against the person (estimate)
likelier: a hard season, a band that keeps close to its shaman, a close choice between two who ask to be heard
rarer: easy years, elders who put little weight on signs, a choice already settled
tone: mixed
life: community, meaning
horizon: moment
roles: elder, rival, friend, partner
tribal: as the band weighs who will be heard at the fire, a sign comes, and every face turns to you
scene tribal: The band sits close around the council fire to weigh who will be heard this winter. Out of the dusk a hawk stoops low and leaves a feather turning at {Ns} feet, and every voice stops.
scene tribal W: There is a custom for this, as for everything: a sign belongs to the elders to read, not to the one it falls beside. {N} keeps still and waits for {elder} to speak.
scene tribal U: {N} watches the faces around the fire more closely than the feather. A hawk hunting at dusk is nothing strange; what the band makes of it is another matter.
scene tribal B: Every eye in the band is on {N}, and {rival} has gone quiet across the fire. A moment like this does not come twice.
scene tribal R: {Ns} heart is pounding. The feather is still rocking in the dust, and {N} wants to snatch it up and speak before the moment cools.
scene tribal G: The hawk has hunted over this valley for as long as {N} can remember. If the spirits are speaking through it, {N} wants to hear what they truly mean.
- W | ask the elders to read the sign by the old custom, and abide by their word | title: local councillor | v: tradition, conformity | self_control: + | chance: 50
- U | slip a second feather into the elders' bundle, so the reading comes out your way | title: local councillor | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: faking a sign before the band; backfire: someone saw the feather planted, and the whole band turns away | v: power, achievement | self_control: - | chance: 50
- B | pick up the feather and tell the band the hawk came for you | act: pick up the feather and tell the band the hawk came for them | title: local councillor | aims: local councillor | identity | v: power, achievement | chance: 50
- R | jump up while every face is turned, and speak from the heart about the winter | title: local councillor | aims: local councillor | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 50
- G | carry the feather to the shaman, and let its meaning come in its own time | title: local councillor | v: tradition | self_control: + | chance: 50
- WUR | say a hunting hawk is no sign, and ask to be judged on your work | identity | grants: a name for straight talk | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 75
- WRG | say the sign fell for your friend, and stand behind your friend instead | mark: turned down a chance | v: benevolence | chance: 80
- WBG | remind the band that your family has spoken at this fire for three generations | grants: a following in the party | v: tradition, power | chance: 60
- UBR | promise the young hunters first share of the next kill for their voices | grants: a loyal campaign team | v: power, achievement | chance: 80
- UBG | say nothing, and watch who looks at the feather and who looks away | grants: counting the votes | v: security, power | chance: 85
works: By the time the fire burns low, the band has settled things the way {N} hoped.
works: The elders nod to {N} across the fire, and the talk of the sign goes on for days.
fails: The elders read the sign another way, and the band's eyes move on to {rival}.
fails: Someone laughs at the wrong moment, and whatever the sign meant is lost in the noise.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 65. the spirits turn from the leader (triads D5b)

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P14): value tags read from the act on 2 options (check.py section 4).
== the spirits turn from the leader
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: mayor | member of parliament | party leader | head of government
per_year: 0 0 .05 .05 .05 .05
drivers: harsh+.4 unrest+.2 prosper-.3 trouble+.15
times: per head of the camp, speaker, faction head or chief in the tribal world a year: about 5 in 100, after a failed hunt or a sickness (estimate)
likelier: a hard winter, a hunt that fails twice running, a sickness in the camp, a rival who keeps the whispering going
rarer: good seasons, a shaman who stands by the leader, a leader who shares the hard choices with the elders
tone: trouble
life: community, meaning
horizon: months
roles: elder, rival, partner, friend
tribal: the herds have not come, the children are sick, and the band whispers that the spirits have turned from you
scene tribal: For the second moon the herds have not come down the valley, and a cough has gone round the hearths. Wherever {N} walks the talk stops, and {rival} is heard saying the spirits no longer walk with the one who leads.
scene tribal W: {N} has led by the customs the band has always kept. If a rite was missed or a taboo broken, it must be put right in front of everyone.
scene tribal U: {N} goes over every step of the last hunts, the winds and the trails. Herds do not vanish for no reason, and neither do coughs.
scene tribal B: {N} hears the whispers for what they are: {rival} reaching for the place at the head of the fire. The surest answer to hunger is meat, brought home by the one who leads.
scene tribal R: {N} is sick of the whispering and the long faces, and of {rival} smiling through all of it. Sitting by the fire and waiting is the worst of it.
scene tribal G: The seasons turn as they will, lean years after fat ones. {N} wonders whether this is a sign to lead differently, or to let another lead.
- W | perform the rite of asking pardon before the whole band, as custom demands | identity | habit | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 60
- U | follow the herds' old trails for days, and show the band where they went | body: heavy | v: universalism, achievement | self_control: + | chance: 70
- B | swear to bring meat home, and drive the best hunters out over the far ridge | binds | body: heavy | v: achievement, power | chance: 55
- R | accuse a rival at the fire of breaking a hunting taboo before the hunt | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: a charge made without proof; backfire: the rival's kin prove it false, and the band turns on the accuser | v: power, security | chance: 65
- G | step down, and let the band choose another to lead through the lean time | drops: mayor; member of parliament | identity | v: tradition | mark: gave in to pressure | chance: 90
- WUG | sit with the shaman and the old hunters until they agree where the herds went | door | v: tradition, universalism | chance: 65
- WUB | share out the stored meat by strict rule, with a tally the whole band can see | v: security, conformity | self_control: + | chance: 75
- WBR | call the band to the fire, and dare any doubter to say it to your face | identity | v: power | chance: 65
- URG | move camp to cleaner ground by the river, and take the sick to the healer there | body: heavy | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 65
- BRG | go alone to the high rocks for three days, and come back with a vision | body: heavy | mark: took a wild risk | v: power, tradition | chance: 60
works: Before the next moon the mood of the band turns, and the whispering dies away.
works: The herds come back down the valley, and the families speak of {N} with respect again.
fails: The whispering grows louder, and the families start to gather at the fire of {rival}.
fails: The sickness lingers through the winter, and the band remembers who was leading when it came.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 66. the shaman reads your dream (pairs D2a)

== the shaman reads your dream
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: party member | campaign volunteer | local councillor
tenure: 2-100
per_year: 0 0 .01 .01 .01 .01
drivers: community+.2 unrest+.1
times: per faction member, hearth-walker or voice at the fire in the tribal world, of two years or more, a year: about 1 in 100 (estimate)
likelier: a band whose speaker has grown old, a shaman close to the family, a dream told at a feast
rarer: a band with a strong speaker, a shaman of a rival family, someone who keeps their dreams to themselves
tone: joy
life: community, meaning
horizon: months
roles: elder, partner, friend, rival, parent
tribal: you tell the shaman a dream of a great fire, and the shaman says it means the band will send you to the gathering
scene tribal: {N} tells the shaman a dream of a great fire on the plain, with every clan of the valley around it. The shaman listens with closed eyes, then says it plainly: the band will send {N} to speak at the gathering.
scene tribal W: {N} feels the weight of it at once. To speak for the band at the gathering is a duty to every hearth, not an honour to wear.
scene tribal U: {N} turns the dream over in the dark. Was the shaman reading the spirits, or the mood of the band, or both?
scene tribal B: A speaker at the gathering sits with the heads of every clan. {N} begins to count which families would stand behind the shaman's words.
scene tribal R: {N} cannot sleep for the joy of it. The great fire, the plain, the clans: {N} can already feel the heat of it.
scene tribal G: Dreams come when they come, like rain. {N} thinks of {parent}, who was never sent, and of the old way of thanking a shaman with the best of the hunt.
- W | take the shaman's reading to the elders, and ask them to put your name forward | title: parliamentary candidate | aims: member of parliament | v: conformity, tradition | chance: 55
- U | ask the shaman for a second sign before believing the first | v: self-direction | chance: 85
- B | go to each family head alone, and say what a speaker could do for them | title: parliamentary candidate | aims: member of parliament | v: power, achievement | chance: 60
- R | stand up at the fire that night and tell the band the dream yourself | title: parliamentary candidate | aims: member of parliament | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 60
- G | bring the shaman the best of your kill, so the reading is told at every hearth | title: parliamentary candidate | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: a gift for a louder reading; backfire: the elders learn of the gift, and the dream counts for nothing | v: tradition, power | chance: 50
- BG | remind the families that your line has spoken for the band before | grants: a following in the party | v: tradition, power | chance: 65
- BR | call in every gift the families owe you, and ask for their voices | grants: allies in the party | v: power | chance: 65
- UR | tell the dream as a story at every hearth, and watch who leans in | door | grants: canvassing | v: stimulation, achievement | chance: 85
- WG | ask your partner and kin whether the hearth can spare you for a summer | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 85
- WU | thank the shaman, and say the band must choose its speaker in the open | mark: turned down a chance | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 85
works: The band takes the dream to heart, and things move the way {N} hoped.
works: By the new moon the families are talking about {N}, and most of the talk is kind.
fails: The elders say a dream is only a dream, and the talk moves on to other hearths.
fails: {rival} hears of the reading and laughs at it by every fire, and the band laughs along.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 67. a feast to win the families (pairs D2b)

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P14): value tags read from the act on 1 option (check.py section 4).
== a feast to win the families
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: council candidate | parliamentary candidate | party leader
once: yes
per_year: 0 0 1 1 1 1
drivers: prosper+.2 harsh-.2
times: per candidate or faction head in the tribal world: once a candidacy, before the gathering (estimate)
likelier: a contested choice, a good season with stores to spare, a rival who has already feasted the band
rarer: a lean year, a choice nobody contests
tone: mixed
life: community, money
horizon: months
roles: rival, partner, elder, friend
tribal: the gathering is a moon away, and the families will follow whoever feasts them best
scene tribal: The gathering is a moon away, and {rival} has already feasted half the band on smoked fish and honey. The families are waiting to see what {N} will put by the fire.
scene tribal W: Custom is clear: one who asks to speak for the band feeds the band. {N} reckons what is fair to every hearth, no more and no less.
scene tribal U: {N} counts the stores twice: the dried meat, the furs, the shells. Every basket given now is a basket the winter will not have.
scene tribal B: A feast is a bargain made in public. {N} wants to know which families' voices count, and what each one will cost.
scene tribal R: {N} can already hear the drums and smell the meat over the fire. If there is to be a feast, it should be one the valley talks about for years.
scene tribal G: The feasts of {Ns} grandmother are still remembered: the first meat of the season, the elders served first. Some ways are old because they work.
- W | give a fair feast by custom, an equal share for every hearth | grants: good name in town | v: conformity, tradition | chance: 75
- U | count the stores, keep enough for winter, and feast the band on the rest | v: security, achievement | chance: 85
- B | feast only the families whose voices will count at the fire | grants: allies in the party | v: power | mark: made an enemy | chance: 75
- R | give it all: every skin and basket, one great night by the fire | takes: a campaign war chest | grants: a following in the party | v: achievement, stimulation | self_control: - | chance: 70
- G | feast the families the old way, with the first meat and the elders served first | habit | v: tradition | chance: 70
- RG | take the young hunters out, and feast the band on what you bring home | body: heavy | grants: a loyal campaign team | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 70
- UB | borrow stores from kin, and keep a careful tally of what is owed | binds | grants: a campaign war chest | v: power, security | chance: 80
- UG | refuse the custom: the stores belong to the winter, and the band knows it | identity | mark: turned down a chance | v: security, universalism | chance: 55
- WB | let the families who bring the most stand nearest the fire | grants: donors | v: power | chance: 75
- WR | invite the families of your rival as well, and serve them first | grants: friends across the aisle | door | v: benevolence, universalism | chance: 55
works: The feast is talked about at every hearth, and the families lean toward {N}.
works: When the gathering comes, the families remember who fed them, and how.
fails: The feast runs thin before the night is half over, and the families drift back to the fire of {rival}.
fails: The band eats well and says kind things, and then follows whoever it was going to follow anyway.

# ================================================================ magic world
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 68. the oracle names you (triads D6a)

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P14): value tags read from the act on 1 option (check.py section 4).
== the oracle names you
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: member of parliament | local councillor | mayor
tenure: 2-100
per_year: 0 0 .01 .01 .01 .01
drivers: era+.3 fortune+.1
times: per member of the Assembly, town councillor or burgomaster in the magic world, of two years or more, a year: about 1 in 100 (estimate)
likelier: a court that keeps an oracle, a time of change at the top, a name already spoken in the Assembly
rarer: a quiet reign, an Order that distrusts prophecy, a name nobody at court knows
tone: mixed
life: work, meaning
horizon: years
roles: boss, rival, mentor, partner, colleague
magic: the oracle of the high tower speaks your name in front of the whole court
scene magic: At the midsummer audience the oracle of the high tower lifts its veiled head and, in a voice like wind through a bell, speaks {Ns} name. It says {N} will rise. The whole court turns to look.
scene magic W: {N} wants nothing done in a hurry. A prophecy spoken at court belongs to the court and the faction to weigh, not to one member with hopes.
scene magic U: {N} knows the oracle's old sayings by heart, and how many came true only in a sideways sense. The exact words matter.
scene magic B: By evening three lords who never knew {Ns} name have sent invitations to dine. {N} notes every one of them.
scene magic R: The blood rushes to {Ns} face, and {N} has to stop from laughing aloud. Rise to what, and when?
scene magic G: Some things are woven before anyone is born. {N} wonders whether this is one of them, or only an old voice in a tower.
- W | tell the faction at once, and let its lord decide what to make of it | v: conformity | chance: 85
- U | find out what the oracle asks of those it names, before doing anything else | v: self-direction, security | chance: 80
- B | let the court believe it, and gather the favours that come with it | grants: friend in power | door | habit | v: power | mark: made a friend | chance: 75
- R | laugh it off before the whole court, and say your fate is your own | v: self-direction | chance: 90
- G | go home to the ward, and let what is meant to come find its way | v: tradition | chance: 85
- WUR | speak out against any office given by prophecy, your own included | mark: turned down a chance | grants: a name for straight talk | v: universalism | chance: 65
- WBR | make the most of the stir, and speak in every hall while the realm listens | grants: known across the country | v: power, achievement | chance: 12
- WBG | pledge the faction your loyalty, so that the prophecy rises with it | grants: allies in the party | v: security, conformity | chance: 70
- URG | take the prophecy to heart, and ask the throne for a seat on its council | title: minister | requires: member of parliament | without: impossible | aims: minister | mark: took a wild risk | takes_if_fails: allies in the party | v: achievement, stimulation | chance: 25
- UBG | say nothing, and quietly learn who at court now fears you | grants: counting the votes | v: power, security | chance: 80
works: The court's attention settles where {N} wants it, and the prophecy works in {Ns} favour.
works: A year on, people still speak of the day the oracle named {N}, and doors open that were shut before.
fails: The prophecy turns sour at court, and the lords who dined with {N} stop sending invitations.
fails: Months pass and nothing rises, and {rival} starts calling {N} the oracle's fool.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 69. a bargain with something old (triads D6b)

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P14): value tags read from the act on 2 options (check.py section 4).
== a bargain with something old
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: parliamentary candidate | member of parliament | party leader
tenure: 1-100
per_year: 0 0 .005 .005 .005 .005
drivers: unrest+.2 stress+.2 trouble+.15
times: per candidate, member of the Assembly or faction head in the magic world, of a year or more, a year: about 1 in 200; most refuse, and few who accept are found out (estimate)
likelier: a close race, a desperate year, old barrows near the city, a house that has bargained before
rarer: a safe seat, the Order's wards near the house, a calm year
tone: mixed
life: work, meaning
horizon: years
roles: partner, rival, grandparent, friend
magic: in the barrow on the night before the lots, a voice offers you the Assembly, and asks for something later
scene magic: On the night before the lots {N} walks out past the city wall to think, and from under the old barrow a voice says {Ns} name. It offers the seat in the Assembly, sure as sunrise, and asks only for something later.
scene magic W: There are laws about such voices, older than the Assembly itself. {N} knows exactly what the Order says about bargains under the hill.
scene magic U: {N} listens to every word with great care. Things under hills are bound by what they say, and so is anyone who answers.
scene magic B: Tomorrow the lots may go either way. Here is a certainty, and {N} has never turned down a certainty without hearing the price.
scene magic R: The hair stands up on {Ns} arms. Part of {N} wants to run, and part wants to shout yes into the dark just to see what happens.
scene magic G: The barrow was old when the city was a ring of huts. {N} remembers the stories {grandparent} told about people who made deals with what sleeps there.
- W | tell the Order what lies under the hill, and let its wardens deal with it | mark: turned down a chance | v: conformity, security | chance: 85
- U | answer with a promise worded so cleverly that it can never come due | title: member of parliament | mark: took a wild risk | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 35
- B | make it name the full price first, and promise nothing yet | v: power | chance: 75
- R | accept: the seat tomorrow, and whatever it asks later | title: member of parliament | aims: member of parliament | binds | mark: took a wild risk | closed: law: a pact with an old power, forbidden by the Order; backfire: the Order finds the mark of it, and the seat is stripped | v: stimulation, achievement | chance: 70
- G | leave bread and salt at the barrow's door, and go home without an answer | v: tradition | chance: 80
- WUG | bind it by oath on its old name: the seat, at a price you set | title: member of parliament | binds | mark: took a wild risk | closed: law: a pact with an old power, forbidden by the Order; backfire: the Order's court, and the seat lost | v: security, tradition | chance: 45
- WUB | refuse, and win the lots the long way, with every pledge counted twice | grants: counting the votes | v: achievement, conformity | self_control: + | chance: 70
- WRG | go home, tell your partner everything, and decide together by morning | v: benevolence | chance: 85
- UBR | ask for the seat and a following in the faction, and haggle hard over the price | title: member of parliament | grants: a following in the party | binds | mark: took a wild risk | closed: law: a pact with an old power, forbidden by the Order; backfire: the Order finds the mark of it, and the seat and the following are lost | v: power | chance: 70
- BRG | refuse, and fight for every lot with your own people and your own strength | grants: a loyal campaign team | identity | v: achievement, self-direction | self_control: + | chance: 70
works: By the time the urns are opened, {N} is sure the choice was right, whatever comes later.
works: The lots fall the way {N} hoped, and the city wakes as if nothing happened in the night.
fails: The lots go against {N}, and the barrow is silent when {N} goes back.
fails: Word of the night under the hill reaches the Order, and {N} is called to explain.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 70. a binding oath of office (pairs D1a)

