== a binding oath of office
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 21-95
holds: minister | mayor | head of government
tenure: 0-1
once: yes
per_year: 0 0 1 1 1 1
drivers: era+.1
times: per councillor of the Crown, burgomaster or Chancellor in the magic world: once, on taking the office, where an Order keeps the old oath (estimate)
likelier: an old city, an office the Orders founded, a realm that remembers an oath-breaker
rarer: a new town without an Order, a lesser office the Crown fills by letter
tone: mixed
life: work, meaning
horizon: years
roles: mentor, boss, partner, rival, colleague
magic: the Order's mages bring the old oath of office, and the words burn as you read them
scene magic: Three mages of the Order carry in the old oath of office, cut in a slab of dark stone. As {N} reads it aloud the words glow, and {N} feels each one settle on {Ns} shoulders like a hand.
scene magic W: An oath is what makes an office more than a chair. {N} has waited years to say these words and means every one of them.
scene magic U: {N} reads ahead while speaking. The fourth clause is broader than anyone said, and nobody seems to have read the sixth in a hundred years.
scene magic B: The oath binds whoever swears it. {N} wonders who else in the hall has sworn it, and how carefully.
scene magic R: The words burn on the tongue. {N} has never liked promises that cannot be taken back, and these cannot.
scene magic G: The first holders of the office swore these same words by the old well, before the city had walls. {N} feels the weight of all of them.
